A||||7||2.8-4spd||Filling luggage rack holes?||||5||
Z||000000||2.8-4spd||11-22-2001||08:40 PM||||I have a 85 Se that Iam putting  a Dodge Shadow spoiler on, but i first have to get rid of the luggage rack. Is there a good way to fill all the holes? Fiberglass? What should I use? Or should I do what I think would be best and find a lid with no luggage rack. I dont mind spending the time on it, I just dont want cracks showing up after i get it painted. Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||8Ball||11-23-2001||08:33 AM||||I would get a lid without the luggage rack if you can.||||reg||1
Z||000002||~*David*~||11-23-2001||09:23 AM||||The "get another deck lid" is good advice! I filled mine and had the car painted.. they look pretty bad and I sanded, sanded and wet sanded! I was successful with another area, a small crack on the fender, but the back lid, close up, well, you can tell it's been worked on..and I sanded my little heart out.||||reg||7
Z||000003||deceler8||11-23-2001||09:54 AM||||I'd go to your hardware store and get some plastic plugs that fit the holes...these usually are black but will take paint fairly well.<P>Might be a cheap and easy way to solve your problem.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deceler8_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||jimmybpei||11-23-2001||08:56 PM||||when you fill them with fiber glass you must dish them out to about 2" . <P>This worked perfect on mine, that is if you have a good body man as well.<P>Later<BR>Jimmy B.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||David DeVoe||11-25-2001||07:13 PM||||Hey 2.8 What year Shadow are you getting your wing from and how do you think it will look on your car. I have an 86 SE with the way ugly lugage rack too and that baby has to go holes or no holes. BTW how hard was it to find that Shadow wing???<BR>DAve||||reg||5
Z||000006||Banzai||11-27-2001||06:55 AM||||I will have a plain decklid off an 84' available in a couple of weeks. I bought a new lid and wing for mine and sold my "good paint" luggage rack lid for $50 plus their old decklid. I haven't seen the other lid yet but I think it just needs paint. $50 plus shipping and it's yours.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bill DCat||11-27-2001||02:38 PM||||I put fiberglass cloth on the bottom of the holes I could get to.  I stuffed the holes I couldn't get to with cotton balls  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Then I filled the tops of the holes with fiberglass resin. After that set up, I used a little body putty on top of the filled holes to taper it out to about a 2" circle.  Sanded everything smooth and painted the decklid.  Turned out pretty well.<P>But, in hindsight, I agree that it would have been easier to just buy one that didn't have the holes in it from a junkyard.||||reg||1
